'''Dragon Priests''' were once the loyal servants of the ancient [[Skyrim:Dragon|dragons]] of [[Lore:Skyrim|Skyrim]]. They ruled over countless armies of men in their gods' names. They are now found residing in coffins throughout [[Skyrim:Nordic Ruins|areas]] of prominent dragon worship. If their sleep is disturbed, the Dragon Priest will burst out of its coffin with considerable force and prepare to destroy whomsoever intruded upon their resting place. 

In combat, Dragon Priests are incredibly dangerous and can kill even high-level players quite quickly. They will constantly backpedal at a high speed, making it difficult to land any melee strikes until the Dragon Priest is driven into a corner. While moving, they will attack with various staves and destructive spells, making for an effective opponent both offensively and defensively.

Dragon Priests are at the high end of the leveled list of possible [[Skyrim:Draugr|draugr]]-type spawns (see [[Skyrim:Leveling#Effects of Leveling|effects of leveling]] for a description of how creatures are generated according to the player-character's level). Because of this, other radiant named bosses, such as [[Skyrim:Curalmil|Curalmil]] and [[Skyrim:Red Eagle|Red Eagle]], may also appear as Dragon Priests if at a high enough level. These enemies will not carry an enchanted mask, however.

When one is close enough to a Dragon Priest sarcophagus, it will burst open forcefully. All random Dragon Priests' sarcophagi are horizontal, so that the lid bursts vertically. When a Dragon Priest is killed, it falls to the ground and almost immediately turns into a pile of ash. The clothing remains intact and is still searchable for loot.
