==Named Dragon Priests==
{{SkyrimBox/Start|text-color=black|main-color=#FBEFD5}}
There are eight named Dragon Priest bosses in the province of Skyrim, each of which wear an [[Skyrim:Dragon Priest Mask|eponymous mask]] with a powerful effect. Each of the eight is challenging in their own way and has access to powerful spells, staves, and certain dragon shouts. Some, but not all, of these Dragon Priests are associated with particular quests. The [[Skyrim:Dragonborn|Dragonborn]] expansion adds five new named Dragon Priests, four of which carry unique enchanted masks (the exception being [[Skyrim:Vahlok the Jailor|Vahlok the Jailor]]).

===In Skyrim===
{{NewLeft}}
====Hevnoraak====
[[File:SR-creature-Hevnoraak.jpg|thumb|Hevnoraak attacking|left]] [[File:SR-item-Hevnoraak.jpg|thumb|The mask of Hevnoraak|right]] Hevnoraak is encountered in [[Skyrim:Valthume|Valthume]] as the final boss in the [[Skyrim:Evil in Waiting|Evil in Waiting]] quest. Hevnoraak is sealed away by [[Skyrim:Valdar|Valdar]], who uses all his power to keep the ancient evil at bay. 


For more information on the creature, see [[Skyrim:Hevnoraak (creature)|this]] article. <br>
For more information on the item of the same name, see [[Skyrim:Hevnoraak (item)|this]] article.
{{NewLeft}}

====Krosis====
[[File:SR-creature-Krosis.jpg|thumb|Krosis in a magical blizzard|left]] [[File:SR-item-Krosis.jpg|thumb|The mask of Krosis|right]] Krosis is located at the clifftop [[Skyrim:Dragon Lairs|dragon lair]] aptly named [[Skyrim:Shearpoint|Shearpoint]]. He is located just in front of the [[Skyrim:Word Wall|word wall]] that reveals every word of the [[Skyrim:Throw Voice|Throw Voice]] [[Skyrim:Dragon Shouts|dragon shout]]. If you have completed [[Skyrim:Dragon Rising|Dragon Rising]], a leveled [[Skyrim:Dragon|dragon]] will spawn here as well. 


For more information on the creature, see [[Skyrim:Krosis (creature)|this]] article.<br>
For more information on the item of the same name, see [[Skyrim:Krosis (item)|this]] article.
{{NewLeft}}

====Morokei====
[[File:SR-creature-Morokei.jpg|thumb|Morokei wielding the [[Skyrim:Staff of Magnus|Staff of Magnus]]|left]] [[File:SR-item-Morokei.jpg|thumb|The mask of Morokei|right]] Morokei is encountered in the ancient ruins of [[Skyrim:Labyrinthian|Labyrinthian]], which can only be accessed during the [[Skyrim:The Staff of Magnus|related quest]]. Morokei is a formidable opponent as he bears the [[Skyrim:Staff of Magnus|Staff of Magnus]]. 


For more information on the creature, see [[Skyrim:Morokei (creature)|this]] article.<br>
For more information on the item of the same name, see [[Skyrim:Morokei (item)|this]] article.
{{NewLeft}}

====Nahkriin====
[[File:SR-creature-Nahkriin.jpg|thumb|Nahkriin, moving away from the portal to [[Skyrim:Sovngarde (place)|Sovngarde]]|left]] [[File:SR-item-Nahkriin.jpg|thumb|The mask of Nahkriin|right]] Nahkriin is encountered guarding [[Skyrim:Alduin|Alduin's]] portal to [[Skyrim:Sovngarde (place)|Sovngarde]] on the top of [[Skyrim:Skuldafn|Skuldafn]] during the quest [[Skyrim:The World-Eater's Eyrie|The World-Eater's Eyrie]]. He wields the [[Skyrim:Dragon Priest Staff (Nahkriin)|staff]] needed for opening the portal.


For more information on the creature, see [[Skyrim:Nahkriin (creature)|this]] article.<br>
For more information on the item of the same name, see [[Skyrim:Nahkriin (item)|this]] article.
{{NewLeft}}

====Otar the Mad====
[[File:SR-creature-Otar the Mad.jpg|thumb|Otar the Mad defending his resting place|left]] [[File:SR-item-Otar.jpg|thumb|The mask of Otar the Mad|right]] Otar the Mad is encountered in the Nordic ruin of [[Skyrim:Ragnvald|Ragnvald]], which is just north of [[Skyrim:Markarth|Markarth]], during the [[Skyrim:Ragnvald (quest)|related quest]]. He is found guarding a [[Skyrim:Word Wall|word wall]] which reveals one word of the [[Skyrim:Kyne's Peace|Kyne's Peace]] [[Skyrim:Dragon Shouts|dragon shout]]. To access his sarcophagus, you must defeat his two keepers, [[Skyrim:Guardian Torsten|Torsten]] and [[SKyrim:Guardian Saerek|Saerek]], each of whom have Skull Keys which are used to unblock Otar's sarcophagus.


For more information on the creature, see [[Skyrim:Otar the Mad|this]] article. <br>
For more information on the item, see [[Skyrim:Otar|this]] article.
{{NewLeft}}

====Rahgot====
[[File:SR-creature-Rahgot.jpg|thumb|Rahgot cloaked in flames|left]] [[File:SR-item-Rahgot.jpg|thumb|The mask of Rahgot|right]] Rahgot is located in the southeastern ruin of [[Skyrim:Forelhost|Forelhost]] during the quest [[Skyrim:Siege on the Dragon Cult|Siege on the Dragon Cult]]. He is partially protected by four common variants of leveled [[Skyrim:Draugr|draugr]].


For more information on the creature, see [[Skyrim:Rahgot (creature)|this]] article.<br>
For more information on the item of the same name, see [[Skyrim:Rahgot (item)|this]] article.
{{NewLeft}}

====Vokun====
[[File:SR-creature-Vokun.jpg|thumb|Vokun with magic seeping out of his ancient robes|left]] [[File:SR-item-Vokun.jpg|thumb|The mask of Vokun|right]] Vokun is encountered in the Nordic ruins of [[Skyrim:High_Gate_Ruins|High Gate Ruins]], in [[Skyrim:The Pale|the Pale]], during the quest [[Skyrim:A Scroll For Anska|A Scroll For Anska]]. He is found guarding an ancient [[Skyrim:Word Wall|word wall]] for the [[Skyrim:Storm Call|Storm Call]] [[Skyrim:Dragon Shouts|dragon shout]]. The battle is made slightly less challenging because [[Skyrim:Anska|Anska]] will fight him, even if the player doesn't.


For more information on the creature, see [[Skyrim:Vokun (creature)|this]] article.<br>
For more information on the item of the same name, see [[Skyrim:Vokun (item)|this]] article.
{{NewLeft}}

====Volsung====
[[File:SR-creature-Volsung.jpg|thumb|Volsung standing before a Word Wall|left]] [[File:SR-item-Volsung.jpg|thumb|The mask of Volsung|right]] Volsung is found on the exterior peak of [[Skyrim:Volskygge|Volskygge]], in northwestern Skyrim, during the [[Skyrim:Volskygge (quest)|related quest]]. He is found guarding a [[Skyrim:Word Wall|word wall]] which teaches one of the words for the [[Skyrim:Whirlwind Sprint|Whirlwind Sprint]] [[Skyrim:Dragon Shouts|dragon shout]]. It is possible to skip the entire dungeon of Volskygge and just ride up the mountain on a horse; however the quest directs otherwise.


For more information on the creature, see [[Skyrim:Volsung (creature)|this]] article.<br>
For more information on the item of the same name, see [[Skyrim:Volsung (item)|this]] article.
{{NewLeft}}

===In Solstheim{{DB}}===
====Ahzidal====
[[File:SR-creature-Ahzidal.jpg|thumb|left|Ahzidal surrounded by his kills]] [[File:SR-item-Ahzidal.jpg|thumb|right|The mask carried by Ahzidal]]
Ahzidal is found entombed in [[Skyrim:Kolbjorn Barrow|Kolbjorn Barrow]], which can only be accessed through the quest [[Skyrim:Unearthed|Unearthed]]. He is awoken and fed the souls of hired [[Skyrim:Miner|miners]] by the subliminally enthralled [[Skyrim:Ralis Sedarys|Ralis Sedarys]]. 

For more information on the creature, see [[Skyrim:Ahzidal (creature)|this]] article.<br>
For more information on the item of the same name, see [[Skyrim:Ahzidal (item)|this]] article.
{{NewLeft}}

====Dukaan====
[[File:SR-creature-Dukaan.jpg|thumb|left|Dukaan wreathed in frost magic]] [[File:SR-item-Dukaan.jpg|thumb|right|The mask carried by Dukaan]]
Dukaan is entombed within [[Skyrim:White Ridge Sanctum|White Ridge Sanctum]], guarding the ancient power of the [[Skyrim:Cyclone|Cyclone]] [[Skyrim:Word Wall|word wall]]. 

For more information on the creature, see [[Skyrim:Dukaan (creature)|this]] article.<br>
For more information on the item of the same name, see [[Skyrim:Dukaan (item)|this]] article.
{{NewLeft}}

====Miraak====
[[File:SR-npc-Miraak 02.jpg|thumb|left|Miraak in Apocrypha]] [[File:SR-item-Miraak.jpg|thumb|right|The mask carried by Miraak]]
Miraak is the primary antagonist in the [[Skyrim:Dragonborn|Dragonborn]] expansion. He was a Dragon Priest when the dragons ruled Tamriel and sought to be free of them. He is mainly seen in [[Lore:Hermaeus Mora|Hermaeus Mora]]'s daedric realm of [[Lore:Apocrypha|Apocrypha]]. He is also Dragonborn, giving him the ability to devour the soul of a dragon and eliminate the chance of it ever returning. Technically, Miraak is an NPC rather than a Dragon Priest creature.

For more information on the NPC, see [[Skyrim:Miraak (person)|this]] article.<br>
For more information on the item of the same name, see [[Skyrim:Miraak (item)|this]] article.
{{NewLeft}}

====Vahlok the Jailor====
[[File:SR-creature-Vahlok the Jailor.jpg|thumb|left|Vahlok the Jailor preparing to attack]]
Vahlok the Jailor is encountered in [[Skyrim:Vahlok's Tomb|Vahlok's Tomb]] during the quest [[Skyrim:Lost Legacy|Lost Legacy]]. He was tasked with watching the traitorous [[Skyrim:Miraak (person)|Miraak]], after discovering Miraak's secret plot against their masters. Vahlok is the only named Dragon Priest who does not have an eponymous mask.

For more information, see [[Skyrim:Vahlok the Jailor|this]] article.
{{NewLeft}}

====Zahkriisos====
[[File:SR-creature-Zahkriisos.jpg|thumb|left|Zahkriisos using his deadly spells]] [[File:SR-item-Zahkriisos.jpg|thumb|right|The mask of Zahkriisos]]
Zahkriisos is encountered in [[Skyrim:Raven Rock Mine|Raven Rock Mine]] during the quest [[Skyrim:The Final Descent|The Final Descent]]. He has the ability to summon [[Skyrim:Seeker|Seekers]] from the daedric realm of [[Lore:Apocrypha|Apocrypha]], and excels in [[Skyrim:Destruction|Destruction]] magic, particularly lightning-based spells. Having [[Skyrim:Resist Shock|Resist Shock]] potions is highly recommended when battling Zahkriisos, as they will greatly reduce the damage inflicted by these spells.

For more information on the creature, see [[Skyrim:Zahkriisos (creature)|this]] article.<br>
For more information on the item of the same name, see [[Skyrim:Zahkriisos (item)|this]] article.
{{NewLine}}
