==Bromjunaar Sanctuary==
[[File:SR-interior-Bromjunaar Sanctuary.jpg|thumb|The Mask pedestals inside the Sanctuary]] In the center of ground-level [[Skyrim:Labyrinthian|Labyrinthian]] lies a small weathered dome. Within is a weathered altar with pedestals for each of the eight Dragon Priest masks. Next to the altar is a [[Skyrim:Wooden Mask|wooden mask]] beside a skeleton. When it is equipped, and the player is inside the dome, the player will be transported back to a time when it was in its prime. When all eight of the unique Dragon Priest masks have been collected, the player can place them all on their respective pedestals. Doing this will reveal the ninth, most powerful, and final mask: [[Skyrim:Konahrik|Konahrik]].

For more information, see the [[Skyrim:Bromjunaar Sanctuary|Bromjunaar Sanctuary]] article.

{{NewLine}}

==Notes==
[[File:SR-creature-Dragon Priest Dead.jpg|thumb|right|A dead Dragon Priest]]
*All Dragon Priests turn to ash upon death, the sole exception being Miraak, who turns into a skeleton instead.
*In terms of stats, [[Skyrim:Malkoran's Shade|Malkoran's Shade]] is considered to be a Dragon Priest, although its level is only 26 and its health is only 300.
*Some named [[Skyrim:Draugr|Draugr]], most notably [[Skyrim:Red Eagle|Red Eagle]], [[Skyrim:Warlord Gathrik|Warlord Gathrik]], and [[Skyrim:Yngol's Shade|Yngol's Shade]], may appear as Dragon Priests at higher levels. This is determined by the [[Skyrim:Radiant|radiant]] system.
*The only location in the game where a Dragon Priest will reliably respawn is [[Skyrim:Forelhost|Forelhost]], after killing Rahgot. Each time the ruin respawns, a new generic Dragon Priest will spawn in Rahgot's place.

